{
  "description": "How an API reads an identifier (contracts/api-conventions.md, \"References to other resources\"; owner decision 2026-10-22). body: a reference to another resource in a request body takes only that resource's prefixed ID. A UUID there, in any case, is 400 invalid_request with the issue at the field: \"use the <noun>'s ID (<prefix>_…)\". Anything else that isn't a prefixed ID of the referenced type (another type's prefix, a malformed value, a non-string) is 400 at the field: \"must be <article> <prefix>_ ID\". issue is null when the value is read; whether the resource exists is checked after. filter: a list filter naming another resource (a query parameter) takes the prefixed ID too: a UUID, in any case, is the same 400 at the parameter; any other value is read as the filter (issue null), and one that isn't a known ID of the type matches nothing (an empty page, never 400 or 503). path: a resource's own path segment takes its prefixed ID or its lowercase UUID; an organization or project segment takes its prefixed ID (org_…, prj_…) or its lowercase UUID (owner decision 2026-11-04); an aliasable segment (Keys' :key) takes those two or alias:<name>. accepted false is the same 404 as a missing resource.",
